ASK {
    math:InformationMeasure logic:subClassOf math:MathematicalObject .
    math:Entropy logic:subClassOf math:InformationMeasure .
    math:MutualInformation logic:subClassOf math:InformationMeasure .
    math:KullbackLeiblerDivergence logic:subClassOf math:InformationMeasure .
    math:CrossEntropy logic:subClassOf math:InformationMeasure .
    math:FisherInformation logic:subClassOf math:InformationMeasure .
    math:Surprisal logic:subClassOf math:InformationMeasure .
    math:JointDistribution logic:subClassOf math:Distribution .
    math:LogarithmBase logic:subClassOf math:MathematicalObject .
    math:InformationUnit logic:subClassOf math:MathematicalObject .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The information-theoretic coverage family MUST keep each measure a specialization of math:InformationMeasure, keep a mutual information's operand a math:JointDistribution specializing math:Distribution, and keep the logarithm base and information unit first-class mathematical objects. These canonical logic:subClassOf edges prevent entropy, divergence, and Fisher information from collapsing into a single untyped scoring token and exercise the exact semantic edges the completeness restrictions and competency frame rely on." .

